      },
      "source": [
        "## Effect of Number of Features (Curse of Dimensionality)\n",
        "\n",
        "We compare KNN using two features and all four features. KNN depends on distance calculations. When the number of features becomes very large, distances may become less useful for distinguishing samples. This is called the *curse of dimensionality*.\n",
        "\n",
        "This small Iris example demonstrates the effect of adding features; it is an illustration, not proof that accuracy must decrease whenever features are added.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 7,
      "id": "92f3dd7f",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "92f3dd7f",
        "outputId": "f4439986-3ce5-4179-b22e-47cb47745938"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Accuracy using 2 features: 100.0 %\n",
            "Accuracy using 4 standardized features: 100.0 %\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "# Use all four features\n",
        "X_all = iris.data\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train_all, X_test_all, y_train_all, y_test_all = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X_all, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Standardize all four features\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train_all)\n",
        "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test_all)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Train KNN using all four features\n",
        "knn_all = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=3)\n",
        "knn_all.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train_all)\n",
        "\n",
        "y_pred_all = knn_all.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
        "accuracy_all = accuracy_score(y_test_all, y_pred_all)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Accuracy using 2 features:\", round(accuracy * 100, 2), \"%\")\n",
        "print(\"Accuracy using 4 standardized features:\", round(accuracy_all * 100, 2), \"%\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
