        "id": "f9014e3c"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Observations\n",
        "1. KNN classifies a sample based on the classes of its nearest neighbours.\n",
        "2. The value of K affects the classification accuracy.\n",
        "3. A very small K can be sensitive to noise, while a larger K may smooth the decision.\n",
        "4. Feature scaling is important because KNN uses distance calculations.\n",
        "5. Adding more features can affect distance measurements. Very high-dimensional data may lead to the curse of dimensionality.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Result\n",
        "The K-Nearest Neighbors classifier was implemented successfully on the Iris dataset. The classification was visualized, different K values were compared, and the effect of using two and four features was observed.\n"
      ]
    }
